diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..b9a2d2f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,17 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "<string>" | null}`: one
+  page of items, ordered by `id` ascending.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100; defaults to 20.
+  - `cursor` (optional): the `next_cursor` value from a previous response;
+    treat it as opaque. Omit it for the first page.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. Walk every page by passing each
+    `next_cursor` back as `cursor` until it is `null`.
+  - An invalid `limit` or `cursor` returns 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
+  - Breaking change: `GET /items` with no parameters used to return every
+    item. It now returns the first 20; pass `limit=100` (the maximum) or walk
+    the pages to get the rest.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
